### Auth (A1, A2)

### 1. A1 Sign up shara (expect 201, id, username shara, role USER, no password)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shara", "password": "shara12345" }

### 2. A1 Sign up shara again (expect 409, "username shara is taken")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shara", "password": "shara12345" }

### 3. A1 Invalid fields (expect 400, two fieldErrors: username and password)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "Lee!", "password": "short" }

### 4. A2 Log in as admin (expect 200, accessToken; kept as adminToken)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "admin1234" }

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 5. A2 Log in as sura (expect 200; kept as suraToken)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "sura", "password": "sura1234" }

> {% client.global.set("suraToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 6. A2 Log in as kenny (expect 200; kept as kennyToken)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "kenny", "password": "kenny1234" }

> {% client.global.set("kennyToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 7. A2 Wrong password (expect 401, "wrong username or password")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "sura", "password": "wrongpass" }

### Courses (P1–P5)

### 8. P2 All courses, no login (expect 200, 3 courses)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses

### 9. P2 Filter: taskLimit at least 5 (expect 200, 2 courses: DB101, WEB101)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses?minTaskLimit=5

### 10. P2 Filter below 1 (expect 400, "minTaskLimit must be at least 1")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses?minTaskLimit=0

### 11. P2 Filter that is not a number (expect 400, "'minTaskLimit' has the wrong type")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses?minTaskLimit=abc

### 12. P3 One course (expect 200, ASP101)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1

### 13. P3 Missing course (expect 404, "course 99 not found")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/99

### 14. P1 Admin creates a course (expect 201 + Location: /api/courses/4)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "code": "NET101", "name": "Networks", "taskLimit": 4, "instructor": "Professor Choi", "credits": 3 }

### 15. P1 No token (expect 401, "login required")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "OS101", "name": "Operating Systems", "taskLimit": 4, "instructor": "Professor Han", "credits": 3 }

### 16. P1 Rule D: a user creates a course (expect 403, "admin role required")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

{ "code": "OS101", "name": "Operating Systems", "taskLimit": 4, "instructor": "Professor Han", "credits": 3 }

### 17. P1 Invalid fields (expect 400, fieldErrors for code, name and taskLimit)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "code": "x", "name": "", "taskLimit": 0, "instructor": "Professor Han", "credits": 3 }

### 18. P1 Code already used (expect 409, "course code ASP101 is taken")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "code": "ASP101", "name": "Copy", "taskLimit": 3, "instructor": "Professor Lee", "credits": 3 }

### 19. P4 Admin renames course 4 and keeps its own code (expect 200)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/courses/4
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "code": "NET101", "name": "Computer Networks", "taskLimit": 5, "instructor": "Professor Choi", "credits": 3 }

### 20. P4 Code of another course (expect 409, "course code DB101 is taken")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/courses/4
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "code": "DB101", "name": "Computer Networks", "taskLimit": 5, "instructor": "Professor Choi", "credits": 3 }

### 21. P4 Missing course (expect 404, "course 99 not found")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/courses/99
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "code": "NET102", "name": "Nothing", "taskLimit": 5, "instructor": "Professor Choi", "credits": 3 }

### 22. P4 Rule D: a user changes a course (expect 403, "admin role required")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/courses/4
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

{ "code": "NET101", "name": "Sura's Networks", "taskLimit": 20, "instructor": "Professor Choi", "credits": 3 }

### 23. P5 Rule D: a user deletes a course (expect 403, "admin role required")
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/courses/4
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

### 24. P5 Course that has tasks (expect 409, "course 1 has tasks")
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 25. P5 Course without tasks (expect 204)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/courses/3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 26. P5 Missing course (expect 404, "course 99 not found")
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/courses/99
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Tasks (C1–C6)

### 27. C2 Tasks of course 1, no login (expect 200, 5 tasks with courseName and ownerUsername)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/tasks

### 28. C2 Missing course (expect 404, "course 99 not found")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/99/tasks

### 29. C1 kenny adds a task to course 1 (expect 201 + Location: /api/tasks/9, status TODO, owner kenny)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{kennyToken}}

{ "title": "Lab G: Docker", "description": "compose file", "priority": "HIGH", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "dueDate": "2026-12-08" }

### 30. C1 Rule A: sura already has 3 open tasks in course 1 (expect 409, "you already have 3 open tasks in course 1 (limit 3)")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

{ "title": "Lab G: Docker", "priority": "HIGH", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "dueDate": "2026-12-08" }

### 31. C1 Rule B: start after due (expect 400, "startDate must be on or before dueDate")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{kennyToken}}

{ "title": "Backwards", "priority": "LOW", "startDate": "2026-12-08", "dueDate": "2026-12-01" }

### 32. C1 Invalid fields (expect 400, fieldErrors for title and dueDate)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{kennyToken}}

{ "title": "", "priority": "LOW", "startDate": "2026-12-01" }

### 33. C1 No token (expect 401, "login required")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Anonymous", "priority": "LOW", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "dueDate": "2026-12-08" }

### 34. C1 Missing course (expect 404, "course 99 not found")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/99/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{kennyToken}}

{ "title": "Nowhere", "priority": "LOW", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "dueDate": "2026-12-08" }

### 35. C3 sura's tasks (expect 200, 5 tasks, all ownerUsername sura)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

### 36. C3 No token (expect 401, "login required")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/mine

### 37. C4 sura reads own task 1 (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

### 38. C4 Rule C: sura reads kenny's task (expect 403, "task 6 belongs to another user")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/6
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

### 39. C4 Admin reads kenny's task (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/6
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 40. C4 Missing task (expect 404, "task 99 not found")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/99
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

### 41. C5 sura moves own task 1 to DOING (expect 200, status DOING)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

{ "title": "Lab F: JWT login", "description": "Finish the login endpoint and the token check", "priority": "HIGH", "status": "DOING", "startDate": "2026-11-20", "dueDate": "2026-11-27" }

### 42. C5 Rule C: sura changes kenny's task (expect 403, "task 6 belongs to another user")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/6
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

{ "title": "Lab E: security", "priority": "MEDIUM", "status": "DONE", "startDate": "2026-11-18", "dueDate": "2026-11-25" }

### 43. C5 Rule C: owner only, so the admin is refused too (expect 403, "task 1 belongs to another user")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "title": "Changed by admin", "priority": "LOW", "status": "DONE", "startDate": "2026-11-20", "dueDate": "2026-11-27" }

### 44. C5 Rule A: sura reopens DONE task 4 while already at 3 open (expect 409, "you already have 3 open tasks in course 1 (limit 3)")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/4
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

{ "title": "Midterm revision", "description": "Weeks 1 to 7", "priority": "LOW", "status": "TODO", "startDate": "2026-10-12", "dueDate": "2026-10-20" }

### 45. C5 Rule B: start after due (expect 400, "startDate must be on or before dueDate")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{suraToken}}

{ "title": "Lab F: JWT login", "priority": "HIGH", "status": "DOING", "startDate": "2026-11-30", "dueDate": "2026-11-27" }

